      "id": "grammar-intentar-infinitive",
      "kind": "grammar",
      "promptEs": "intentar + infinitivo",
      "questionEn": "How do you say that someone tries to do an action?",
      "answerEn": "Use a form of intentar followed directly by the action verb in its unchanged dictionary form.",
      "noteEn": "No linking preposition is needed between the two verbs. Intento abrir means “I try to open,” and intentamos salir means “we try to leave.” The attempted action stays in its basic -ar, -er, or -ir form.",
      "example": {
