      "kind": "grammar",
      "promptEs": "me arreglan el móvil · van a lavarle el coche",
      "questionEn": "How can Spanish identify the person affected through a body part, possession, or other closely connected noun without putting a possessive word before it?",
      "answerEn": "Mark the affected person with me, te, le, nos, or les, then use el, la, los, or las before the closely connected noun.",
      "noteEn": "The short person word goes before a changed verb, as in le repararon, or attaches to an unchanged -ar, -er, or -ir form, as in repararle. The article matches the related noun, whether it names a body part, possession, service, or closely associated aspect. Natural English often expresses that relationship with my, your, his, her, our, or their.",
      "example": {
        "es": "Van a lavarle el coche a Ana.",
        "en": "They are going to wash Ana's car."
